{"id":"leather","name":"Leather","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:leather"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Leather","text":"A girdle of, worn by Elijah (2 Kings 1:8) and John the Baptist (Matt. 3:4). Leather was employed both for clothing (Num. 31:20; Heb. 11:37) and for writing upon. The trade of a tanner is mentioned (Acts 9:43; 10:6, 32). It was probably learned in Egypt."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"G1193","lemma":"δερμάτινος","xlit":"dermátinos","gloss":"made of hide","kjv":"leathern, of a skin","count":2,"share":0.25},{"strong":"G66","lemma":"ἄγριος","xlit":"ágrios","gloss":"wild , literally or figuratively","kjv":"wild, raging","count":2,"share":0.25},{"strong":"G1038","lemma":"βυρσεύς","xlit":"byrseús","gloss":"a tanner","kjv":"tanner","count":2,"share":0.25},{"strong":"G4613","lemma":"Σίμων","xlit":"Símōn","gloss":"Simon , the name of nine Israelites","kjv":"Simon","count":3,"share":0.38},{"strong":"H5785","lemma":"עוֹר","xlit":"ʻôwr","gloss":"skin","kjv":"hide, leather, skin","count":3,"share":0.38},{"strong":"G200","lemma":"ἀκρίς","xlit":"akrís","gloss":"a locust","kjv":"locust","count":2,"share":0.25}],"verses":["Matt.3.4","Mark.1.6","Gen.3.21","Lev.8.17","2Kgs.1.8","Acts.9.43","Acts.10.5","Acts.10.6"],"related":[{"id":"tanning","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.375,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"}],"works":[{"work":"stern1862","title":"Wanderings among the Falashas in Abyssinia","count":7,"chapters":[{"chapter":"Stern.2","count":2,"book":"Stern 1862","title":""},{"chapter":"Stern.3","count":2,"book":"Stern 1862","title":""},{"chapter":"Stern.20","count":2,"book":"Stern 1862","title":""},{"chapter":"Stern.11","count":1,"book":"Stern 1862","title":""}]},{"work":"anf04","title":"Ante-Nicene Fathers, Volume 4: Tertullian (Part Fourth), Minucius Felix, Commodian, Origen (Parts First and Second)","count":6,"chapters":[{"chapter":"ANFXXI.3","count":4,"book":"Origen Against Celsus","title":"Book III"},{"chapt